{"duration_api_ms":27950,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8956ad7d-b2e7-4c87-8e3d-1d1bcf5c8621","total_cost_usd":2.2965652,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273042,"cache_read_input_tokens":261566,"output_tokens":2995,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1097},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273042,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":551,"cache_read_input_tokens":261566,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11476},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2995,"cacheReadInputTokens":261566,"cacheCreationInputTokens":273042,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2965652,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1097,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json`. Lena Gonzalez / `egi-draft-a1v2` is coded **rung 2: \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"** It rests on two passages that are one record, her vote on AB 1955 (2023-2024).\n\n- **Vote page:** she voted Aye on the Senate floor on 2024-06-13 (actor `Glazer, Gonzalez, Hurtado`, tally `PASS, 29-8`). The vote is in her current term. 8 of 37 voted No, so it is not near-unanimous.\n- **Bill text:** Section 220.5(a) of the chaptered text, quoted as `provision_quote`, says schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require\" disclosure of a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2.\n- **Not rung 1:** the bill only removes any duty to disclose (Section 220.3). It does not require staff to keep the information from parents, which is what rung 1 needs.\n\n**Judgement calls to check:**\n\n- **Preemption:** I coded it `on-question`, not `adjacent` under H12. The bill does forbid local rules, but rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules, so the H12 exception applies.\n- **Single subject:** I treated AB 1955 as single-subject (pupil-privacy). It also funds resources for parents of LGBTQ pupils and bars retaliation against staff, but all of that is the same subject. If a reviewer calls it multi-subject, the row falls to direction only.\n\nThere are no quotes in her own words and no `needs_source` entries.","ttft_ms":11668,"type":"result","duration_ms":30115,"uuid":"6081da08-f504-4edc-8727-c37a1dfb4cc7","ttft_stream_ms":1795,"time_to_request_ms":101,"first_content_frame_ms":1795,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
